      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having deduped lists in `mm_struct` and `files_struct` doesn\u0027t mean there aren\u0027t duplicates between them. I agree the copying isn\u0027t ideal. It\u0027d be possible to do it without allocating by scanning the MM list for each FD, but that\u0027s not so great either.\n\nFor an O(1) implementation, all of this type of work gets moved to mmap/unmap/allocate/free time, but I think I might have a way to avoid the multiple lists. More news later this week...",
